/-!
# Globally semiample normalized adjoints glue on an sdlt threefold

Let `(T, Δ; L)` be a projective sdlt adjoint pair of pure dimension three over `ℂ`, with
normalization components `νᵢ : Tᵢ ⟶ T` carrying the boundaries `Θᵢ = Cᵢ + Δᵢ`, so that the
normalized component adjoints are `Lᵢ = ν^*L|_{Tᵢ} = K_{Tᵢ} + Θᵢ`. If every `Lᵢ` is semiample,
then `L` is semiample on the whole of `T`: some Cartier multiple `mL` is generated by its global
sections at every point of `T`, the conductor included.

The proof passes to crepant projective `ℚ`-factorial dlt models of the `(Tᵢ, Θᵢ)`, generates the
adjoints of the surface components of their floors by admissible systems in a common even degree,
lifts these to preadmissible systems on the threefold models, and descends those through the
conductor to sections of `𝒪_T(mL)`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.IsSdltAdjointPair.exists_isAdjointGeneratorOn_of_isRelativelySemiample`.

## Implementation notes

As in `MMP.Fourfold.IsSdltAdjointPair`, a section of `𝒪_T(mL)` is a family `t = (tᵢ)ᵢ` of
rational `m`-canonical forms on the normalization components which is, near every point of `T`,
the product `ν^*f · g` of a function `f` on an open `U ⊆ T` and a local generator `g` of
`𝒪_T(mL)` on `U` (`MMP.Fourfold.IsAdjointGeneratorOn`). Such a section generates `𝒪_T(mL)` at
`x` when it is itself a local generator on a neighbourhood of `x`. Semiampleness of `L` is the
existence of `m > 0` with `mΔ` integral such that global sections generate `𝒪_T(mL)` at every
point. Semiampleness of `Lᵢ` is `MMP.Fourfold.QDivisor.IsRelativelySemiample` over `Spec ℂ` of
`K_{Tᵢ} + Θᵢ` for a canonical divisor `K_{Tᵢ}`; it does not depend on the choice of `K_{Tᵢ}`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, *Singularities of the minimal model program*][Kollar2013], Section 5.1
-/

@[expose] public section

section

